from mkchar import write
write("Hester_Maharala","Hester Maharala","0","1","6","Books 1, 2, 3, 6 (chapter files)","Emir_Bahadir.md, Constance.md, ../04_Peoples_and_Cultures/Pranay_Culture.md",
 "Emir's portal user and head of logistics, born in Jayapura in Pranay.",
 "- Emir directs \"a woman named Hester\" to open a portal for the Boko rescue; she traces a circle in the air and the portal shimmers (Book 1, Ch109 L6). She can only open a portal to places she has visited, and the time before her next use depends on range (Book 1, Ch109 L7-9).\n- She is the Asiatic-looking person Jason sees first in this world, closer to South Asian than his own Japanese features (Book 2, Ch34 L55).\n- \"Hester was one of Emir's most important staff members\", in charge of logistics and coordination between his operations (Book 2, Ch69 L64).\n- Born in Jayapura, a port city of Pranay (Book 2, Ch69 L65-66); she has a clifftop house with grotto rooms and a swim-access bar (Book 2, Ch69 L69-72).\n- A shopkeeper calls her \"Hester Maharala... The lady with the house on the hill\" (Book 2, Ch70 L70).\n- Jason compares her portal range to his own shadow portals (Book 3, Ch8 L25); she portals Clive back to the city (Book 3, Ch30 L21) and Emir plans to ask her to portal Callum back (Book 3, Ch69 L186).\n- In Book 6 Gary imagines Hester arriving to portal him to a memorial service (Book 6, Ch47 L172).",
 "Warm, travelled and practical; the one who gets people where they need to be and keeps Emir's operations running.")
write("Korinne_Pescos","Korinne Pescos","0","7","9","Books 7, 9 (chapter files)","Rufus_Remore.md, Jason_Asano.md",
 "A guild-elite team leader who first meets Jason in the Rimaros surge and later asks him to train her team.",
 "- Leader of the guild team in the mixed-force expedition: \"The leader of the guild team, Korinne, moved to them\" (Book 7, Ch47 L54). She tells her angry team member Kalif he does not want to make an enemy of \"the next Amos Pensinata\" (Book 7, Ch47 L59).\n- She relays orders efficiently once her training kicks in, with no sign of the unruliness she had shown earlier (Book 7, Ch48 L16).\n- She defends Jason to others: \"he's our asshole, and we don't turn on our own assholes\" (Book 7, Ch50 L51).\n- Full name Korinne Pescos, leader of Orin and Kalif's team, who had coordinated the underwater complex rescue (Book 9, Ch24 L49-52).\n- In Book 9 she visits Jason's cabin and is guarded about his methods; her team are silver-rank guild elites who \"operated alone through most of the surge\" (Book 9, Ch25 L31-63).\n- She guesses Jason will talk about Rimaros-style versus Vitesse-style adventuring, specialisation versus generalisation (Book 9, Ch25 L58).",
 "Brisk and proud of her team's training; she softens only when someone earns it.")
write("Jonah_Geller","Jonah Geller","0","1","12","Books 1, 2, 9, 12 (chapter files)","Rick_Geller.md, Danielle_Geller.md, Humphrey_Geller.md",
 "A heavy-armoured Geller family fighter on Rick's team who is captured by the Builder cult and dies when the star seed is extracted.",
 "- He challenges Jason in front of Danielle: \"I'm going to show this little no-name weed what it means to fight a Geller\" (Book 1, Ch66 L72-78).\n- On Rick's team he is the bulwark, slowed by heavy armour and a shield (Book 1, Ch67 L14-15); he shouts to draw out monsters (Book 1, Ch67 L66).\n- After the desert astral-space expedition Danielle seeks legal permission from his family to have him examined for a star seed, as he refuses (Book 2, Ch10 L26-50).\n- Humphrey says Jonah had quit Rick's team and was found with a new team in Hornis (Book 2, Ch14 L116).\n- Years later he is remembered as captured, implanted with a star seed by the Builder cult and dead in the extraction; Dustin Kettering took his place on the team (Book 9, Ch1 L39; Book 12, Ch16 L83).",
 "Brash and loyal; the Geller who learned too late what the family name could not protect him from.")
write("Gilbert_Bertinelli","Gilbert Bertinelli","0","1","12","Books 1, 2, 3 (chapter files)","Jason_Asano.md, Gary.md",
 "A Greenstone tailor who sells Jason his combat robe and later suits.",
 "- Runs \"Gilbert's Resilient Attire For the Discerning Gentleman\" and invites customers to call him Bert; one of octuplets named after Berts, including the \"handsome\" Bertrand (Book 1, Ch61 L76-87).\n- Sells Jason the trap-weaver-silk and leather combat attire, haggled by Gary and priced in bronze coins, which is unusual for iron-rank gear (Book 1, Ch61 L92-114).\n- Makes Jason a tuxedo (Book 1, Ch65 L6) and refers him to his brother for specialised desert boots (Book 1, Ch76 L3-5).\n- In Book 3 he has reached iron rank late, having kept all his cloth essence abilities at bronze (Book 3, Ch2 L59-62), and shows Jason a winter wardrobe \"largely in the Vitesse style\" (Book 3, Ch2 L64).\n- Jason's combat robe is \"custom made for him by Gilbert Bertinelli\" (Book 5, Ch30 L58); Gilbert supplied his armour (Book 2, Ch44 L8).",
 "Courtly, theatrical and sharp about quality; he does not hide his rivalry with his brothers.")
write("Ian_Evans","Ian Evans","0","4","13","Books 4, 5, 13 (chapter files)","Erika_Asano.md, Emi_and_Nik.md, Jason_Asano.md",
 "Jason's brother-in-law, Erika's husband and Emi's father, who can enter Jason's spirit vault.",
 "- Jason senses Erika, her husband Ian and their daughter Emi on his return (Book 4, Ch3 L132); the contact is named \"Ian Evans\" (Book 4, Ch3 L123).\n- Jason introduces \"my sister, Erika, her husband, Ian, and their daughter\" to Dr Baudrillard (Book 5, Ch3 L130).\n- Erika and Ian are midway through iron, having taken cores regularly (Book 5, Ch3 L126).\n- Ian is one of only three people outside Jason's blood relatives who can enter his spirit vault; \"I've known Jason since he was twelve years old\" (Book 5, Ch44 L45).\n- Vincent Baudrillard is Emi's boyfriend in Book 13 (Book 13, Ch971 L49); Ian's place in that family is as Emi's father.",
 "Steady and humane; he trusts Jason because he has seen him at his lowest.")
write("Asya_Karadeniz","Asya Karadeniz","0","4","5","Books 4, 5 (chapter files)","Kaito_Asano.md, Greg.md, Anna_Tilden.md",
 "A school friend of Jason's and Network administrator who crews Kaito's helicopter and is killed in Book 5.",
 "- She says she went to school with Jason Asano and is \"just an administrator\" who keeps the people doing the work \"happy and funded\" (Book 4, Ch36 L37-41).\n- She is on Kaito's three-person helicopter crew with Greg (Book 5, Ch7 L12), operating the weapons when a black winged lizard comes into her sights (Book 5, Ch7 L21-23).\n- Her mother Rabia represents the non-Asano families on the Asano Village committee (Book 5, Ch13 L74-75).\n- She enters Jason's spirit vault \"as her relationship with Jason deepened\" (Book 5, Ch44 L45).\n- Anna says of the Berlin deaths: \"The bastards killed Asya\" (Book 5, Ch51 L52); Akari says Kaito, Asya and Greg died fighting for their world (Book 5, Ch51 L40).\n- Her parents and siblings, the Karadeniz family, confront Jason; her mother slaps him (Book 5, Ch56 L24-26).",
 "Sharp, funny and fiercely loyal; her death is a wound the others carry into Book 5.")
write("Greg","Greg","0","1","5","Books 4, 5 (chapter files)","Kaito_Asano.md, Asya_Karadeniz.md, Jason_Asano.md",
 "An old school friend of Jason's who joins Kaito's crew and is killed in Book 5.",
 "- Jason remembers an old school friend Greg who roped him and Amy into long board games (Book 4, Ch7 L42).\n- On Kaito's helicopter crew with Asya (Book 5, Ch7 L12; Ch14 L42).\n- Says he was \"never much more than an adequate lawyer\" and had been pushed out of his father's practice; he had lived more in six months of magic than in six years before (Book 5, Ch58 L14).\n- His family is among those taken in at Asano Village (Book 5, Ch13 L74); Jason later bows his head before Greg's family (Book 5, Ch56 L26).\n- Akari says Kaito, Asya and Greg were fighting for their world (Book 5, Ch51 L40).",
 "Nerdy, self-deprecating and braver than he believed.")
